.TH UWSGI 1 "October 20, 2026" "uWSGI 2.0.31" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uwsgi \- application server with Python WSGI support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uwsgi
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B uwsgi
.I configuration.ini
.SH DESCRIPTION
uWSGI serves Python WSGI applications over HTTP or the uwsgi protocol.
It provides worker process management, request routing, and caching.
Application configuration can be supplied on the command line or in an
INI file containing a [uwsgi] section.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete list of available options.
.TP
.B --version
Print the server version.
.TP
.BI --http-socket " address"
Listen for HTTP requests on the specified address, such as 127.0.0.1:8080.
.TP
.BI --socket " address"
Listen for requests using the uwsgi protocol.
.TP
.BI --wsgi-file " file"
Load a Python WSGI application from the specified file.
.TP
.BI --module " module[:callable]"
Load a Python module and an optional application callable.
.TP
.B --master
Enable the master process, which supervises worker processes.
.TP
.BI --processes " count"
Start the specified number of worker processes.
.TP
.BI --threads " count"
Use the specified number of threads in each worker.
.TP
.B --need-app
Exit if no application can be loaded.
.TP
.B --vacuum
Remove generated sockets and PID files when the server exits.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
uwsgi --http-socket 127.0.0.1:8080 --master --processes 2 \\
      --module myapp:application --need-app --vacuum
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The complete upstream documentation is available at
.UR https://uwsgi-docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/
.UE .
